infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title The seven-tier tradeoff cascade
  desc Each act unlocks the next only if the prior is sound — skip one and you pay for it in every act that follows
  order asc
  sequences
    - label Act 1 — Schema
      desc Wrong keys here poison sharding: skip it and Acts 2–7 fight inefficient joins and mutable natural keys.
    - label Act 2 — Indexing
      desc Without indexes the planner is blind: Act 3 statistics are useless with nothing to choose between.
    - label Act 3 — Statistics
      desc Skip stats and vacuum is your only lever; tables bloat while you guess at cardinality.
    - label Act 4 — Bloat control
      desc Dead tuples inflate heap pages; Act 5 pool threads then see slower table scans.
    - label Act 5 — Pool sizing
      desc Connection storms starve Act 6 migrations; the handshake backlog blocks lock acquisition.
    - label Act 6 — Lock-safe migrations
      desc Without expand-contract, Act 7 is impossible without downtime — every rebalance needs an exclusive lock.
    - label Act 7 — Sharding
      desc Shard only when single-node limits are measured; skip it and one tenant dominates while others queue.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
